      "name": null,
      "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ For all $i\\in Z,$ $5∤i.$\n\n*Hint: Recall that $a∣b$ means \"$a$ divides $b.$\"*",
      "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(i):5∣i,\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∀i\\in Z,\\,¬P(i).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∀i\\in Z,\\,¬P(i)) & ≡∃i\\in Z,\\,¬¬P(i) \\\\  & ≡∃i\\in Z,\\,\\text{ }P(i).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∃i\\in Z,\\,P(i)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **There exists** $i\\in Z$ such that $5∣i.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
