      "problem": "Negate the following statement:\n\n$\\,$ There exists $k\\in Z$ such that $2k$ is not even.",
      "worked_solution": "If we denote\n\n$$\nP(k):2k\\text{ is even},\n$$\n\nour statement can be written as\n\n$$\n∃k\\in Z,\\,¬P(k).\n$$\n\nNegating this, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}¬(∃k\\in Z,\\,¬P(k)) & ≡∀k\\in Z,\\,¬¬P(k) \\\\  & ≡∀k\\in Z,\\,P(k).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, $∀k\\in Z,\\,P(k)$ reads as follows:\n\n$\\,$ **For all** $k\\in Z,$ $2k$ is even.",
